            <ArticleTitle>Catheter-induced left main coronary artery dissection resulting in abrupt closure and cardiac arrest: successful stenting during resuscitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E93-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Catheter-induced left main coronary artery dissection is an uncommon but devastating complication of coronary angiography and percutaneous coronary intervention. We present a case of left main coronary artery dissection induced with a guide catheter, which resulted in acute occlusion and cardiac arrest. Survival and complete functional recovery were achieved with bailout stenting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
